  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Open Ticket",
    "overview": "Wage records are drawn as an issue tracker. Each record is a row that someone owes an answer on, with a deadline running against it. The interface refuses the landing-page arrangement (no hero, story section, stats band, or card grid) because the only job is to let a reviewer register a report, answer as the employer, and read the contract's refusal in under a minute. It is an Operate-mode product surface, dense and calm, in Traditional Chinese.\n\nTokens come from the Linear app system (via the design-md-library reference): a near-black canvas, a four-step charcoal surface ladder, 1px hairlines, and one lavender accent. Geist and Geist Mono stand in for Linear's own faces. Two values were adjusted from the reference for contrast: primary hover is darker (`#4f5bc4`) so white text keeps contrast on hover, and the quietest text is lifted to `#7d828a`.\n\nStatus is the only place colour carries meaning, and it never carries it alone: every status is a drawn icon whose shape differs, paired with a text label. Everything else is greyscale plus a single lavender.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Three-pane tracker: sidebar, grouped list, detail or composer panel.",
      "Flat tonal depth: surfaces step up in lightness, hairlines separate, shadows are nearly absent.",
      "Geist for words, Geist Mono for every ID, amount, hash, block height and clock.",
      "Pending is a pie that fills as the deadline runs out, driven by chain time.",
      "Data is drawn, not decorated: bars, hatched shortfall, deadline track and gate ladder all encode values."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Lavender Is Rare Rule",
        "body": "Lavender appears only on the primary action, the selected row or option (as the wash), and focus. It never colours text, icons, status, links or decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never Colour Alone Rule",
        "body": "A status is always its own icon shape plus a text label (等待回應, 雇主確認, 雇主異議, 逾期未回應). Colour reinforces and is never the sole signal; this is a product accessibility commitment.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Status Colours Are Reserved Rule",
        "body": "The four status hues mean only their status (and, for red and green, the gate ladder and errors that restate it). They are not used as brand or accent colours.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono For Values Rule",
        "body": "Any ID, amount, timestamp, hash or block number is Geist Mono with tabular numerals. Words never are.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence-Case Label Rule",
        "body": "Section and nav headings are 12px to 13px, weight 500, sentence case, in Ink 3 or Ink 4. There are no uppercase tracked eyebrows or kickers in this system.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Not Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Separate regions with a 1px hairline or a one-step surface change. A card never gets a shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** express every status as its own icon shape plus text label; keep the pie filling in real time from chain time.",
